### Pulse — Slice 1 API Tests (Member A)
### VS Code REST Client format
### Prerequisites: Local server running on port 5000 and database populated with 00, 01, 02, 10, 11, 20

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. AUTHENTICATION & LOGIN
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1a. Sign in as Hospital Staff (Anita Kulkarni, City Care Hospital, Pune)
# @name staffLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "STAFF",
  "email": "staff.citycare@example.com",
  "password": "Pulse@123"
}

### Store Staff Token
@staffToken = {{staffLogin.response.body.token}}

### 1b. Sign in as Donor (Aarav Shah - O+, Pune, eligible)
# @name aaravLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "email": "aarav@example.com",
  "password": "Pulse@123"
}

### Store Aarav Token
@aaravToken = {{aaravLogin.response.body.token}}

### 1c. Sign in as Donor (Neha Kulkarni - O+, Pune, donated 30 days ago, ineligible)
# @name nehaLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "email": "neha@example.com",
  "password": "Pulse@123"
}

### Store Neha Token
@nehaToken = {{nehaLogin.response.body.token}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. DONOR PROFILE & COUNTDOWN (Aarav & Neha)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2a. GET /donors/me (Aarav - should show is_eligible: true, days_remaining: 0)
GET {{baseUrl}}/donors/me
Authorization: Bearer {{aaravToken}}

### 2b. GET /donors/me (Neha - should show is_eligible: false, days_remaining: 60 [T19])
GET {{baseUrl}}/donors/me
Authorization: Bearer {{nehaToken}}

### 2c. PUT /donors/me (Aarav updates phone and coordinates)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/donors/me
Authorization: Bearer {{aaravToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9811119999",
  "city": "Pune",
  "latitude": 18.520400,
  "longitude": 73.856700,
  "notify_email": true,
  "notify_sms": true
}

### 2d. GET /donors/me/donations (Aarav donation history)
GET {{baseUrl}}/donors/me/donations
Authorization: Bearer {{aaravToken}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. ELIGIBLE DONORS DIRECTORY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3a. GET /donors/eligible (Staff views eligible directory - no phone/email exposed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/donors/eligible
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. BLOOD REQUESTS & MATCHING
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4a. POST /requests (Staff creates CRITICAL O+ blood request, radius 50km)
### Expected response: 201 { request_id: N, status: "MATCHED", match_count: 3 }
# @name createCriticalRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "request_type": "BLOOD",
  "blood_type_needed": "O+",
  "urgency": "CRITICAL",
  "radius_km": 50,
  "units_needed": 2,
  "patient_name": "Emergency Patient X"
}

### Store Request ID
@createdRequestId = {{createCriticalRequest.response.body.request_id}}

### 4b. GET /requests/:id/matches (Staff lists matched donors nearest-first)
### Expected order: Aarav (0.0 km), Priya (~8.0 km), Rahul (NULL km, same-city)
GET {{baseUrl}}/requests/{{createdRequestId}}/matches
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 4c. GET /requests (Staff views their hospital's requests)
GET {{baseUrl}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 4d. GET /requests?status=MATCHED (Staff filters by MATCHED status)
GET {{baseUrl}}/requests?status=MATCHED
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 4e. GET /requests/critical (Staff views open critical requests)
GET {{baseUrl}}/requests/critical
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. MATCH NOTIFICATION & DONOR RESPONSE [T22]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5a. GET /donors/me/matches (Aarav views matches received)
# @name getAaravMatches
GET {{baseUrl}}/donors/me/matches
Authorization: Bearer {{aaravToken}}

### Store Aarav's Match ID
@aaravMatchId = {{getAaravMatches.response.body[0].match_id}}

### 5b. POST /matches/:id/respond (Aarav responds ACCEPTED to match [T22])
### Expected response: { match_id, contacted_status: "ACCEPTED", responded_on }
POST {{baseUrl}}/matches/{{aaravMatchId}}/respond
Authorization: Bearer {{aaravToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "response": "ACCEPTED"
}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. LOGGING DONATIONS & ELIGIBILITY ENFORCEMENT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6a. POST /donations (Attempt donation for Neha - ineligible, donated 30 days ago)
### Expected response: 409 { error: "...", code: "DONOR_NOT_ELIGIBLE" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/donations
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "donor_id": 6,
  "donation_type": "BLOOD",
  "units": 1
}

### 6b. POST /donations (Valid donation by Aarav linked to request)
### Expected response: 201 { donation_id: N }
### Database trigger marks Aarav ineligible and marks request FULFILLED automatically.
POST {{baseUrl}}/donations
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "donor_id": 1,
  "request_id": {{createdRequestId}},
  "donation_type": "BLOOD",
  "units": 1
}

### 6c. Verify Request is now FULFILLED
GET {{baseUrl}}/requests?status=FULFILLED
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. CANCEL REQUEST
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 7a. POST /requests (Create a MODERATE request to test cancellation)
# @name createCancelRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "request_type": "BLOOD",
  "blood_type_needed": "A+",
  "urgency": "MODERATE",
  "radius_km": 50,
  "patient_name": "Patient for Cancel Test"
}

@cancelRequestId = {{createCancelRequest.response.body.request_id}}

### 7b. PATCH /requests/:id/cancel (Staff cancels open request)
### Expected response: { request_id: N, status: "CANCELLED" }
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/requests/{{cancelRequestId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
